            <ArticleTitle>Clinical management issues in vasculitis. Angiographically defined angiitis of the central nervous system: diagnostic and therapeutic dilemmas.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>S127-30</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of acute neurologic deficit accompanied by a cerebral angiogram consistent with CNS vasculitis is presented. The differential diagnosis and diagnostic decision process generated in this type of evaluation is illustrated.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
